    57	    Server <-->|"OpenAI-compatible /v1 API"| Compiler
    58	    Compiler <-->|"Tool Calls & JSON Responses"| Tools
    59	    Tools <-->|"docker exec / subprocess"| ContA
    60	    ContA -->|"git add -N . && git diff --binary"| ContB
    61	    ContB -->|"exit_code == 0 & JUnit XML valid"| Score["Resolution Rate [0.0, 1.0]"]
    62	```
    63	
    64	---
    65	
    66	## 2. Submission Contract & Declarative Agent Schema (`adk-submission`)
    67	
    68	### 2.1. Declarative-Only Security Model
    69	Competitors **do not** submit Python code entrypoints (`agent.py` or `agent_fn`). Standard ADK's `from_config()` permits arbitrary dynamic Python imports; **`adk-submission` replaces it with a sandboxed YAML compiler (`compile_submission`)**. All agents, sub-agents, workflows, tools, and generation parameters are declared in YAML and resolved against closed host registries (`ToolRegistry`, `ModelRegistry`, `SkillRegistry`, `CallbackRegistry`).
    70	
    71	### 2.2. Submission Directory Layout
    72	A valid submission directory (packaged at the root of `submission.zip`, evaluated by `scripts/inference.py` in Stage 1 to produce `submission.parquet`) follows this layout:
    73	
    74	```text
    75	submission/
    76	├── agent.yaml                  # REQUIRED: Root agent config (or root_agent.yaml; .yml also accepted)
    77	├── eval_config.yaml            # Optional: Per-task evaluation budget & timeout overrides
    78	├── configs/
    79	│   └── sampling.yaml           # Optional: Generation parameters loaded via !include
    80	├── prompts/
    81	│   ├── system.md               # Optional: System instructions loaded via !include
    82	│   └── analyzer.md
    83	├── sub_agents/
    84	│   └── code_analyzer.yaml      # Optional: Sub-agent or AgentTool YAML configurations
    85	├── adapters/                   # Optional: Fine-tuned PEFT LoRA adapters or model weights
    86	│   ├── main_lora/
    87	│   │   ├── adapter_config.json
    88	│   │   └── adapter_model.safetensors
    89	│   └── tool_lora/
    90	│       ├── adapter_config.json
    91	│       └── adapter_model.safetensors
    92	└── skills/                     # Optional: ADK Skill directories (each containing SKILL.md)
    93	    └── repo_navigation/
    94	        └── SKILL.md
    95	```
    96	
    97	- **Root Config Discovery**: Exactly one root config (`agent.yaml`, `agent.yml`, `root_agent.yaml`, or `root_agent.yml`) must exist in the submission root. Having zero root files raises `MissingRootConfigError`; having more than one raises `MultipleRootConfigsError`.
    98	- **Optional Evaluation Budget Config (`eval_config.yaml`)**: Submissions may include an optional `eval_config.yaml` at the root under an `evaluation:` key (`timeout_seconds`, `max_tool_calls`, `max_time_minutes`, `max_turns`) to customize per-task operational budgets during Stage 1 inference (`load_submission_eval_config` in `scripts/inference.py`).
    99	- **Sandboxed `!include` Directive**: YAML files may embed external files using `!include <relative_path>`:
   100	  - `.md` and `.txt` files are loaded as raw UTF-8 strings (ideal for `instruction` or `global_instruction`).
   101	  - `.yaml` and `.yml` files are parsed recursively (up to a maximum include depth of `10` with cycle detection).
   102	  - Absolute paths, null bytes, `..` traversal components, and symlinks resolving outside the submission root are strictly blocked (`PathTraversalError`).
   103	
   104	### 2.3. Supported Agent Classes (`agent_class`)
   105	`SandboxedAgentConfig` supports four discriminated agent types (defaulting to `LlmAgent` if `agent_class` is omitted):
   106	
   107	1. **`LlmAgent` (default)**:
   108	   - `name` (`str`, required): Agent identifier string.
   109	   - `model` (`str`, required unless a default model is set): Model alias from the registry (`gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`, `gemma-4-12b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`, `gemma-4-e4b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`, or `gemma-4-e2b-it-qat-w4a16-ct` for competition submissions).
   110	   - `adapter` (`str | None`): Optional adapter name matching a subdirectory or weight file under `adapters/`.
   111	   - `description` (`str`, up to `1,000,000` chars): Used by parent agents when delegating to this agent.
   112	   - `instruction` (`str`, up to `1,000,000` chars): System prompt for the agent. Supports ADK session state templating (`{problem_description}`, `{hints}`, or custom `output_key` variables).
   113	   - `tools` (`list`): List of tool names (`str`), `AgentTool` references (`agent_tool: {config_path: ..., skip_summarization: true}`), or inline agent dictionaries.
   114	   - `skills` (`list[str] | None`): List of relative paths to skill directories within the submission archive.
   115	   - `sub_agents` (`list`): List of `{config_path: ...}` references for multi-agent transfer.
   116	   - `output_key` (`str | None`): Saves the agent's final text output into `session.state[output_key]`.
   117	   - `include_contents` (`"default" | "none"`): Controls whether conversation history is passed to the agent.
   118	   - `disallow_transfer_to_parent` / `disallow_transfer_to_peers` (`bool | None`).
   119	   - `generate_content_config` (`dict | None`): Sampling, seed, and thinking parameters (see constraints below).
   120	2. **`SequentialAgent`**:
   121	   - Executes `sub_agents` in sequential order. Accepts `name`, `description`, `sub_agents`, and agent callbacks.
   122	3. **`ParallelAgent`**:
   123	   - Executes `sub_agents` concurrently in isolated branches. Accepts `name`, `description`, `sub_agents`, and agent callbacks.
   124	4. **`LoopAgent`**:
   125	   - Repeatedly executes `sub_agents` up to `max_iterations` (`int`, default `500`, bounded to `1..500`).
   126	
   127	### 2.4. Enforced Structural Limits & Generation Constraints
   128	Submission constraints in `swegemma` (`build_submission_limits()` in `swegemma/config.py`) are intentionally minimal: **aside from security sandboxing (no symlinks, no path traversal, declarative YAML only), the primary hard constraint is a total unpacked submission size of `< 3 GiB` (`3,221,225,472` bytes), including all `adapters/` weights**, plus token ceilings required by the 4x L4 GPU context window (`32,768` tokens).
   129	
   130	All other structural limits are set to generous safety ceilings solely to guard against runaway recursion or zip/YAML anchor bombs:
   131	
   132	| Category | Parameter | Competition Limit / Allowed Range |
   133	| :--- | :--- | :--- |
   134	| **Primary Archive Constraint** | **`max_total_size_bytes`** | **`3 GiB` (`3,221,225,472` bytes total unpacked size, including `adapters/`)** |
   135	| **Structural Safety Ceilings (`SubmissionLimits`)** | `max_file_count` | `10,000` files |
   136	| | `max_yaml_files` | `1,000` YAML files |
   137	| | `max_yaml_size_bytes` | `50 MiB` per YAML file / cumulative `!include` expansion |
   138	| | `max_skill_size_bytes` | `50 MiB` per skill directory |
   139	| | `max_instruction_chars` | `1,000,000` chars per agent (`10,000,000` total across all agents) |
   140	| | `max_agents` | `500` total agents in the compiled tree |
   141	| | `max_sub_agent_depth` | `50` levels of nesting (`sub_agents` and `agent_tool`) |
   142	| | `max_skills` | `1,000` skills |
   143	| | `max_loop_iterations` | `500` iterations for any `LoopAgent` |
   144	| | `allowed_file_extensions` | Strictly required formats only: `.yaml`, `.yml` (agent/eval configs), `.md`, `.txt` (prompts & `SKILL.md`), `.py` (ADK skill scripts), `.json` (`adapter_config.json`), and `.safetensors` (`adapter_model.safetensors`). Pickle-based weights (`.bin`, `.pt`, `.pth`) and other binary/archive extensions are rejected. |
   145	| | `adapter_extensions` | `.safetensors` only (`adapters/<name>/adapter_model.safetensors`) |
   146	| **Generation Config (`GenerationConstraints`)** | `allowed_fields` | **All schema fields permitted**: `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`, `max_output_tokens`, `presence_penalty`, `frequency_penalty`, `stop_sequences`, `response_mime_type`, `seed`, `thinking_config` |
   147	| | `max_output_tokens` | `1` to `32,768` (default `16,384`; bounded by 4x L4 vLLM `max_model_len=32768`) |
   148	| | `thinking_config.thinking_budget` | `0` to `32,768` (default `4,096`; bounded by 4x L4 vLLM `max_model_len=32768`; positive values set `enable_thinking: true` and forward `extra_body.thinking_token_budget` to vLLM's `ThinkingTokenBudgetLogitsProcessor`, while `0` sets `enable_thinking: false`) |
   149	| | `thinking_config.thinking_level` | `"MINIMAL"`, `"LOW"`, `"MEDIUM"`, `"HIGH"`, or `"NONE"` (case-insensitive). *Note*: When serving via vLLM's OpenAI-compatible `/v1` endpoint (especially with LoRA adapters), omit `thinking_level` and configure `include_thoughts: true` + `thinking_budget: 4096` instead, because `thinking_level` maps to OpenAI's `reasoning_effort` parameter (`swegemma` also sets `litellm.drop_params = True`). |
   150	| | `thinking_config.include_thoughts` | `true` or `false`. When `thinking_budget > 0` (or `thinking_level` is active), `include_thoughts: true` retains `Part(thought=True)` in `LlmResponse` and subsequent tool-call context (`<\|channel>thought...<channel\|>`), whereas `include_thoughts: false` still enables reasoning on the current turn (`enable_thinking: true`) while stripping `Part(thought=True)` from `LlmResponse` and outgoing message history. When neither `thinking_budget` nor `thinking_level` is set, `include_thoughts` acts as a fallback toggle for `enable_thinking`. |
   151	| | `temperature` / `top_p` / `top_k` / penalties / `seed` / `stop_sequences` | Unrestricted (any valid schema value; `temperature >= 0.0`, `0.0 <= top_p <= 1.0`, `top_k >= 1`; `seed` is forwarded in the outgoing request body to LiteLLM/vLLM) |
   152	
   153	> [!WARNING]
   154	> Execution-altering ADK fields that bypass the sandbox (`tools`, `system_instruction`, `http_options`, `safety_settings`, or `response_schema` inside `generate_content_config`) are excluded from `GenerateContentConfig` by schema design and will raise a validation error if set.
   155	
   156	---
   157	
   158	## 3. Model Registry, Single-Model Rule & LoRA Adapters on 4x L4 GPUs
   159	
   160	### 3.1. Computational Environment: 4x NVIDIA L4 GPUs (96 GB Total VRAM)
   161	The competition evaluation environment runs on a dedicated machine equipped with **4 × NVIDIA L4 GPUs**:
   162	- **Per-GPU Memory**: `24 GB GDDR6` (`96 GB` total VRAM across 4 GPUs).
   163	- **vLLM Serving Configuration (`setup_vllm_server` in `scripts/inference.py`)**:
   164	  - `tensor_parallel_size = 4` (shards model weights and KV cache across all 4 L4 GPUs)
   165	  - `gpu_memory_utilization = 0.90` (`~21.6 GB` usable per GPU / `~86.4 GB` usable across 4 GPUs)
   166	  - `max_model_len = 32768` (`32,768` tokens maximum combined prompt + reasoning + output context length)
   167	  - `scheduler_reserve_full_isl = False`
   168	  - `enable_auto_tool_choice = True`, `tool_call_parser = "gemma4"`, `reasoning_parser = "gemma4"`, `reasoning_config = {"reasoning_start_str": "<|channel>", "reasoning_end_str": "<channel|>"}`
   169	  - Dynamic LoRA right-sizing from discovered adapters: `enable_lora = bool(adapter_map)`, `max_loras = max(1, len(adapter_map))`, `max_lora_rank = max(detected_ranks) if detected_ranks else 128`
   170	  - Model-specific CLI flags (`MODEL_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS`): for `gemma-4-12b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`, passes `--hf-overrides '{"architectures": ["Gemma4ForCausalLM"], "model_type": "gemma4"}'`
   171	
   172	| Base Model Variant | Weight Precision | Approximate Weight Footprint (4 GPUs) | Competition Status |
   173	| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
   174	| **`gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`** *(Starter Kit Default)* | W4A16 (INT4 Quantized) | `~16–18 GB` (`~4.5 GB / GPU`) | **Permitted in Kaggle competition submissions** (`ALLOWED_MODEL_NAMES`) |
   175	| **`gemma-4-12b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`** | W4A16 (INT4 Quantized) | `~6–8 GB` (`~1.8 GB / GPU`) | **Permitted in Kaggle competition submissions** (`ALLOWED_MODEL_NAMES`) |
   176	| **`gemma-4-e4b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`** | W4A16 (INT4 Quantized) | `~3–4 GB` (`~1.0 GB / GPU`) | **Permitted in Kaggle competition submissions** (`ALLOWED_MODEL_NAMES`) |
   177	| **`gemma-4-e2b-it-qat-w4a16-ct`** | W4A16 (INT4 Quantized) | `~2–3 GB` (`~0.7 GB / GPU`) | **Permitted in Kaggle competition submissions** (`ALLOWED_MODEL_NAMES`) |
   178	| **`gemma-4-31b-it` / `gemma-4-27b-it` / `gemma-4-26b-a4b-it` / `gemma-4-12b-it` / `gemma-4-9b-it` / `gemma-4-e4b-it` / `gemma-4-e2b-it`** | `bfloat16` | `~4–62 GB` | Registered in `models.yaml` / `_build_cli_model_registry()` for local CLI evaluation only |
   179	
   180	This 4x L4 hardware budget directly governs four operational rules:

