   202	When the scoring harness starts the local inference server (`setup_vllm_server` in `scripts/inference.py`, running `VllmServer` on `127.0.0.1:8000` with `tool_call_parser='gemma4'`, `reasoning_parser='gemma4'`, `max_model_len=32768`), it binds the declared model alias (and any discovered adapter names) to `LiteLlm(model=f"openai/{served_model}", api_base="http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1")` via `server_instance.create_model_registry(...)` (or fallback `LiteLlm(..., num_retries=3)` when attaching to an already-active endpoint) and installs the LiteLLM reasoning patch (`install_litellm_reasoning_patch()`).
   203	
   204	### 3.4. Multi-LoRA Serving (`adapters/`) & Sizing Guidelines
   205	Even though a submission is restricted to a single base model, **different agents in your hierarchy can use different fine-tuned LoRA adapters**:
   206	1. Place PEFT LoRA directories (containing `adapter_config.json` and `adapter_model.safetensors`) inside `adapters/<adapter_name>/`. Adapter names must match `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*`.
   207	2. Reference `adapter: <adapter_name>` on any `LlmAgent` in `agent.yaml` or `sub_agents/*.yaml` (for example, `adapter: main_lora` on the root coder agent and `adapter: tool_lora` on a read-only analyzer `AgentTool`).
   208	3. `discover_adapters()` automatically registers all discovered adapters with the vLLM server, right-sizing `enable_lora = bool(adapter_map)`, `max_loras = max(1, len(adapter_map))`, and `max_lora_rank = max(detected_ranks) if detected_ranks else 128` (passed under `--lora-modules name1=path1 name2=path2 ...`), and `resolve_swegemma_adapter` (`src/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py`) routes requests from each agent to its respective `openai/<adapter_name>` model identifier.
   209	4. **Adapter Size Planning (`< 3 GiB` total budget)**:
   210	   - For a 31B model in `bfloat16` targeting all linear projections (`q_proj`, `k_proj`, `v_proj`, `o_proj`, `gate_proj`, `up_proj`, `down_proj`):
   211	     - **Rank `r = 16`**: `~110–220 MB` per adapter (easily fits 8 specialized adapters within `< 3 GiB`).
   212	     - **Rank `r = 32`**: `~220–450 MB` per adapter (fits 6–8 adapters within `< 3 GiB`).
   213	     - **Rank `r = 64`**: `~450–900 MB` per adapter (fits 3–6 adapters within `< 3 GiB`).
   214	     - **Rank `r = 128` (`max_lora_rank`)**: `~0.9–1.8 GB` per adapter (fits 1–3 high-rank adapters within `< 3 GiB`).
