param.default` holds that value. If the class implements `__eq__` in a way that relies on comparing attributes, and one of those attributes is a complex object (like a custom class instance), the comparison `param.default == param.empty` might behave unexpectedly if `param.default` is an instance of a class that overrides `__eq__` in a way that makes it equal to `param.empty` (though `param.empty` is a unique sentinel, so this is unlikely unless the default value itself is somehow related to `param.empty` or the comparison is flawed).\n\nHowever, the problem statement says: \"When `repr`ing classes that have overwritten `__eq__` as parameters, the check with `== Parameters.empty` can be `True`.\"\n\nIf `param.default` is an object that overrides `__eq__`, and that object is somehow compared to `param.empty`, it might evaluate to `True` if the object's `__eq__` method is triggered and returns `True` for `param.empty`.\n\n`param.empty` is a unique object provided by `inspect`. If a user provides a default value, say `None`, then `param.default` is `None`. `None == param.empty` is `False`.\n\nIf the default value is a custom object `C`, then `C == param.empty` is evaluated. If `C` implements `__eq__`, it will be called.\n\nThe fix suggested in the issue description (which I don't have, but I must infer the intent) is likely to ensure that we are comparing the default value strictly against the sentinel, perhaps by checking the type or using `is` if `param.empty` is guaranteed to be a singleton (which it is).\n\nLet's check the documentation or common practices for `inspect.Parameter`. `param.empty` is indeed a unique sentinel object.\n\nIf `param.default` is a custom object `C`, and `C.__eq__(param.empty)` returns `True`, then the condition `param.default == param.empty` evaluates to `True`, even if `C` was not intended to be the sentinel.\n\nTo fix this, we should check if `param.default` is *exactly* `param.empty`, not just equal to it.\n\nI will change:\n`if param.default == param.empty:`\nto\n`if param.default is param.empty:`\n\nLet's apply this change in `rich/repr.py`.\n\nThe context around the change:\n```python\n                    elif param.kind in (\n                        param.POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD,\n                        param.KEYWORD_ONLY,\n                    ):\n                        if param.default == param.empty:\n                            yield getattr(self, param.name)\n                        else:\n                            yield param.name, getattr(self, param.name), param.default\n```\n\nI will use `edit_file`.", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 5436, "completion_tokens": 1136, "cached_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 6572}, "model": "/kaggle/input/models/google/gemma-4/other/gemma-4-e4b-it-qat-w4a16-ct/2"}, {"timestamp": 1793892693.9855, "elapsed_s": 227.257, "type": "tool_call", "author": "swe_baseline_agent", "tool": "edit_file", "args": {"filepath": "rich/repr.py", "new_string": "                        if param.default is param.empty:\n                            yield getattr(self, param.name)\n                        else:\n                            yield param.name, getattr(self, param.name), param.default", "old_string": "                        if param.default == param.empty:\n                            yield getattr(self, param.name)\n                        else:\n                            yield param.name, getattr(self, param.name), param.default"}, "model": "/kaggle/input/models/google/gemma-4/other/gemma-4-e4b-it-qat-w4a16-ct/2"}, {"timestamp": 1793892693.9900029, "elapsed_s": 227.261, "type": "tool_response", "author": "swe_baseline_agent", "tool": "edit_file", "result": "{\"status\": \"ok\", \"filepath\": \"rich/repr.py\", \"occurrences\": 1, \"strategy\": \"exact\", \"diff\": \"--- a/rich/repr.py\\n+++ b/rich/repr.py\\n@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@\\n                         param.POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD,\\n                         param.KEYWORD_ONLY,\\n                     ):\\n-               